# AMD X3D (dual-CCD V-cache) CPU: prefer the V-cache CCD for games.
# amd_x3d_mode=cache makes the scheduler rank the V-cache CCD (CPUs 0-5,12-17)
# above the frequency CCD; the firmware default is "frequency". Background jobs
# are already pinned to the other CCD (6-11,18-23).
#
# Why udev and not tmpfiles.d: a tmpfiles `w` line needs the exact device path
# (a firmware-assigned ACPI name) and runs once at boot, so it
# misses a driver rebind or module reload. This rule matches the DRIVER, hard-
# codes no device name, and fires on "add" (boot coldplug, driver already
# bound) and on "bind" (every later driver (re)bind, e.g. modprobe -r/+).
# Installed by fixes/fix_amd_x3d_vcache.sh.
ACTION=="add|bind", SUBSYSTEM=="platform", DRIVER=="amd_x3d_vcache", ATTR{amd_x3d_mode}="cache"
